// Filter controls for the data app in public/, declared once here.
//
// A given is a typed runtime parameter (docs/givens.md). The tags on each
// declaration are its *control contract*: what the input is labelled, which
// widget renders it, and where a picker gets its choices. That contract is a
// property of the declaration, not of any one page, so the same given renders
// identically everywhere it is read, including a notebook's Parameters panel.
//
// Nothing here says *what* gets filtered. data_app.malloy decides that, with a
// `where:` naming the given. That split is why one CATEGORY control can scope
// revenue in one place and margin in another without either redeclaring it.
//
// Declaration order below is control order for anything that reads the model's
// given list: a notebook's Parameters panel and the data app's control row.
//
// Note `# description="…"` and not `#(description="…")`. Malloy has both forms
// and they feed different readers, which is worth knowing before copying either.
// Measured against this server: the plain tag is parsed into `Given.description`
// on the API response, and the bracketed one is not, arriving instead as a raw
// string in `annotations`. The bracketed form is what the notebook Parameters
// panel renders as helper text today, and it also makes the compiler warn
// `malformed-route`, because a route runs to the first space. The two are read
// independently and neither overwrites the other, so a model with both readers
// can carry both. This model's reader is public/index.html, which takes the
// parsed field, so it carries one. See docs/givens.md §Annotations.
##! experimental.givens

// `control=select` with a `suggest` renders a picker whose options come from
// the data. A `source=`/`dimension=` pair reads distinct values off a source.
# description="Narrow to one product category. Leave empty for all"
# label="Category" control=select suggest { source=products dimension=category }
given: CATEGORY :: filter<string> is f''

// `multiselect` lets a reader pick several at once. Here the options come from
// a named query rather than a source, which is the form to reach for when the
// list needs its own ordering or filtering.
# description="One or more brands. Leave empty for all"
# label="Brand" control=multiselect suggest { query=brand_suggest dimension=brand }
given: BRAND :: filter<string> is f''

# description="Narrow to one US sales region. Leave empty for all"
# label="Region" control=select suggest { source=regions dimension=region }
given: REGION :: filter<string> is f''

// A plain (non-filter) `date` renders as a date picker. The storefront data
// runs 2023-01-01 through 2025-12-31, so this default takes in all of it.
# description="Only count orders placed on or after this date"
# label="Ordered since"
given: SINCE :: date is @2023-01-01

// Numeric bounds turn a `filter<number>` into a slider instead of a text box.
# description="Ignore line items below this sale price"
# label="Minimum line total" range_min=0 range_max=250
given: MIN_SALE :: filter<number> is f''
